INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction to the Importance of Determining Melon Seed Rate per Hectare</h2>\n<p>For every farmer, finding the balance between seed cost and final crop yield is a primary challenge. In the case of <strong>the amount of melon seed per hectare</strong>, this balance is more critical than for many other crops because melon requires sufficient space for root and fruit development. If seed density is too high, plants will compete with each other and fruit quality will decline. Conversely, if density is too low, field coverage will be incomplete and yield will decrease. Therefore, understanding calculation formulas and planting factors is the first step toward profitability. Additionally, understanding the relationship between planting density and water management is key to successful melon cultivation.</p>\n\n<h2>Factors Influencing the Determination of Melon Seed Rate per Hectare</h2>\n<h3>Seed Variety Type and Seed Size</h3>\n<p>Different melon varieties differ in seed size and Germination Rate. Hybrid varieties usually have a higher Germination Rate, which results in a lower required seed dose. However, one must always adhere to the recommendations on the seed packet label. When using older seeds or open-pollinated varieties, it may be necessary to slightly increase the seed dose to ensure an appropriate final plant density in the field. For a better understanding of the relationship between seeds and spacing, you can also refer to the seed rate per hectare guide, which explains similar principles for sowing other varieties. Attention to these points helps prevent the purchase of excess seed.</p>\n\n<h3>Planting Method and Final Spacing</h3>\n<p>The largest factor that affects <strong>the watermelon seed rate per hectare</strong> is the final furrow and row spacing. In modern agriculture, these spacings are designed for drip irrigation systems. If the main row spacing is 2 meters and the sub-row spacing is 60 centimeters, you can calculate the number of seedlings that can be planted by calculating the space per square meter. As planting spacing decreases, the number of seedlings per hectare increases. Therefore, care must be taken to ensure that the seed spacing is appropriate for these final spacings to minimize the need for thinning. These calculations form the basis of proper farm management.</p>\n\n<h2>Calculating the precise watermelon seed dose</h2>\n<h3>Basic formula and conversion factors</h3>\n<p>For precise calculation, the following standard formula is used: Plants per hectare = (1,000,000 / (main row spacing × sub-row spacing)). After determining the required number of plants, divide it by the seed germination percentage and then multiply by the weight of one thousand seeds. For example, if your seeds have a 90% germination rate, divide the initial dose by 0.9. Finally, use standard coefficients to convert units. These precise calculations prevent buying excess or insufficient seed. In this context, familiarity with <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/raining-pipes-types-and-uses/">types of irrigation pipes</a> also helps align the irrigation system with planting density.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ملون-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ملون در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare for watermelon crop</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n<h3>Impact of drip and subsurface drip irrigation systems</h3>\n<p>In drip irrigation systems, seeds are planted immediately adjacent to the drip emitters. This method is widely adopted due to optimal water use efficiency and the reduction of root diseases. If you use a subsurface drip irrigation system, seeds are planted at a depth of approximately 5 to 10 cm to protect them from water splashing and thermal stress. In watermelon cultivation using these systems, precision in planting depth and distance from irrigation lines is of particular importance. For more information on the proper installation of these systems, refer to the page titled \'Key Points Before Installing Subsurface Drip Irrigation in the Field.\' Complete coordination between seed and water ensures product quality.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical tips for planting and fertilization</h2>\n<h3>Planting time and seed conditions</h3>\n<p>Watermelon planting time must be scheduled so that the plant coincides with favorable weather conditions during the fruit production stage. Watermelon seeds are sensitive to soil temperature and germinate poorly in cold soil. Always use fresh seeds with high germination rates. Additionally, soak seeds before planting to promote faster germination. When using imported seeds or specific cultivars, the seed rate may vary. Precision in timing completes half the work.</p>\n\n<h3>Manual and mechanized seed sowing</h3>\n<p>For large farms, using mechanized seeders ensures higher precision. These machines typically allow for the adjustment of depth and seed count. If you use manual sowing, ensure that seeds are placed uniformly in the holes or along the row. In some cases, the use of simpler models such as <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%db%8c%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%aa-%da%af%d9%84%d8%b1%d9%86%da%af-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%87%da%a9%d8%aa%d8%a7%d8%b1/">Cucurbita maxima yield estimation guide</a> This helps you gain a better understanding of plant canopy density at soil level. Uniform planting is the key to consistent crop yield.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Thinning and reducing plant density</h3>\n<p>Even with high precision, it may be necessary to reduce plant numbers after germination. If two plants are too close together, remove one to ensure sufficient space for fruit development. Removing extra plants during early stages reduces competition for water and nutrients. In drip irrigation systems, this step is critical because an extra plant will waste water. Timely thinning guarantees final quality.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ملون-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ملون در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>Melon crop seed rate per hectare</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions about melon seed quantity per hectare</h2>\n<h3>Does the seeding rate vary with different varieties?</h3>\n<p>Yes, seed size and germination percentages differ among various cultivars. Therefore, always check the seed label and adjust the standard formula with the specific coefficient for your seed. This is a point often overlooked by new farmers.</p>\n\n<h3>Should planting distance be adjusted based on soil type?</h3>\n<p>Heavier soils generally require more space for root development. Therefore, in clay soils, increase the row spacing slightly and reduce density. Adaptation to local conditions is essential.</p>\n\n\n<h3>What is the optimal sowing depth for melon seeds?</h3>\n<p>The ideal depth is 2 to 4 centimeters. Sowing too deep slows growth, while surface sowing exposes seeds to damage from wind and rain. Maintaining the proper depth promotes faster growth.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقدار-بذر-ملون-در-هکتار-راهنمای-جامع-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقدار بذر ملون در هکتار: راهنمای جامع - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>Seed rate per hectare for melon crop</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>Proper Selection <strong>Melon seed rate per hectare</strong> This is a combined process involving mathematical calculations, seed variety recognition, and coordination with the irrigation system. By applying the provided formulas and observing the mentioned practical guidelines, you can prevent seed waste and achieve high yields. It is recommended to perform a trial calculation on a small section of the field before starting planting to determine the optimal density for your specific conditions.</p>\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> Important considerations before installing drip tape in the field, <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/millet-seed-quantity-per-hectare-guide/">millet seed quantity per hectare guide</a></p>\n<p><strong>Related Articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%86%da%a9%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%85%d9%87%d9%85-%d9%82%d8%a8%d9%84-%d8%a7%d8%b2-%d9%86%d8%b5%d8%a8-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be-%d8%af%d8%b1-%d9%85%d8%b2%d8%b1%d8%b9%d9%87/">Important considerations before installing drip tape in the field</a></p>','Colored Seed Quantity per Hectare: A Comprehensive Guide for Farmers','This article provides a precise guide for calculating watermelon seed requirements per hectare. It covers everything from mathematical calculations to practical planting tips using drip and tape irrigation systems.','publish','closed','closed','colored-seed-quantity-per-hectare-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
